{"title":"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba1ea2ff1caf77831140b0a5972314412f47af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, x_3, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"11\" /> be a sequence of positive integers defined as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd241834905de5246fcbb2444ed65f963fccbce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> and for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6821383bad74988bdb3845a6cea48b40aea81f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{n+1}=x_n+\\lfloor\\sqrt{x_n}\\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> Determine all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for which there exists some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340797a8fa9f1a06b10ce9e764998830b15ca755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/30214ba5d940687b09852b6db27ada82fead34b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n = m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />. (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for every real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.)\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>This problem needs a solution! Please help by adding a solution.\nWe have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e97c4d2b30f783254737ce7fdf1ac0c2fd93c306.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1=1,\\qquad x_{n+1}=x_n+\\lfloor \\sqrt{x_n}\\rfloor .\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We want to determine all positive integers \\(m\\) such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91b519126abe8877c5d337a1fdfd5f8bef5db64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_n=m^2\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>for some \\(n\\ge1\\).\n</p><p>The answer will be\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/97414fb8995237a9db7b3a74cae23e7542d734b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{m=2^k\\qquad(k=0,1,2,\\ldots)}\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Solution:\n</p><p>Suppose at some point we reach\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91b519126abe8877c5d337a1fdfd5f8bef5db64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_n=m^2\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>for some positive integer \\(m\\).\n</p><p>We will prove the following key lemma:\n</p><p>Lemma: If \\(m^2\\) occurs in the sequence, then the next square occurring in the sequence is \\((2m)^2\\), and there is no square between them.\n</p><p>Once this is proved, the whole problem is immediate.\n</p><p>Step 1: Understand what happens inside one interval\n</p><p>Suppose\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20cb5b8f320c409e1bcadd0d290f17d396cd9ce2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k^2\\le x&lt;(k+1)^2.\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/c/f6c7a4fbc7268a446e8e0fe6e044773a55a0cdca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor\\sqrt{x}\\rfloor=k,\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>so the recurrence becomes simply\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfa328bf70f30a8cc86ee2e73082d56337d8ef8c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{\\text{next}}=x+k.\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63d45183c4768aaf46f9622ab753c7baf37b254c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=k^2+r,\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>where\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/a/49a3c8a2dbff789126f745f52678faadf16302ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0\\le r\\le 2k.\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/2/f427938964be010530abc9f0dc9bf6c63c4c004d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{\\text{next}}=k^2+r+k.\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>There are two cases.\n</p><p>Case 1: \\(0&lt;r\\le k\\)\n</p><p>Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3d11892524b79bd268c8b4593156776fb88cee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r+k\\le2k,\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>so we are still in the same interval \\([k^2,(k+1)^2)\\).\n</p><p>After one more step,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec2510cc14106a7c64548c375934dc1d092d45e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x&#39;=k^2+r+2k.\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Since \\(r&gt;0\\),\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/19011120c691869c17170971d528fd0ecb8dd049.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r+2k&gt;2k,\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>so we pass \\((k+1)^2\\).\n</p><p>The new value is\n</p>\n<pre style=\"color:red\">\\begin{aligned} x&#39; &amp;=k^2+r+2k\\\\ &amp;=(k+1)^2+(r-1). \\end{aligned} (Error compiling LaTeX. Unknown error_msg)</pre>\n<p>Therefore:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/8/2881d03eb14bd003744ad39df1e0772f558dc7fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{k^2+r\\longrightarrow (k+1)^2+(r-1)}\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>after two steps.\n</p><p>So the quantity \\(r\\) decreases by \\(1\\), while \\(k\\) increases by \\(1\\).\n</p><p>Case 2: \\(r=0\\)\n</p><p>This is the important case where we are exactly at a square:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4b21c8d11263529e88bbc4fcb78b18ced16997.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=k^2.\\]\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/4/4548595c9e37428f55428ac29551fb2bf719c58b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k^2\\to k^2+k=k^2+k,\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8cd9f9ed8f4b1b0e2efce0d14cb0b59ee6cc2bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k^2+k\\to k^2+2k=(k+1)^2-1.\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>One more step gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08b92a21370062cf5c9f0a64799e4fb57ada19b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(k+1)^2-1+k =(k+1)^2+(k-1).\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Hence\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b7776c75473652cb3090bdbe4e863ec30c4b58.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{k^2\\longrightarrow (k+1)^2+(k-1)}\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>after three steps.\n</p><p>Step 2: Start from \\(m^2\\)\n</p><p>Now assume\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29e5a276a53ba2803b8c23607fe5f391c7109c96.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_n=m^2.\\]\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>By Case 2, after three steps we arrive at\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a463cfe69210d1e51b63f808538b53d977a09e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(m+1)^2+(m-1).\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>So, in the interval corresponding to \\(k=m+1\\), the remainder is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/984ccd014f0cdb4c30760f3de31e909f209204f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=m-1.\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Since \\(r&gt;0\\), Case 1 applies.\n</p><p>After two steps, we enter the next interval with remainder\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/4092167d9ec42a15e1729b0992272e95249b96ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m-2.\\]\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Then another two steps gives remainder\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/6/bf6cfa33c1be7ed8ef1092875360adefb6f094bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m-3.\\]\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Continuing in this way:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d51d1e34f6d88f3b4cb5358cb658574151e73ec5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c} \\text{interval} &amp; \\text{remainder} \\\\ \\hline (m+1)^2\\le x&lt;(m+2)^2 &amp; m-1\\\\ (m+2)^2\\le x&lt;(m+3)^2 &amp; m-2\\\\ (m+3)^2\\le x&lt;(m+4)^2 &amp; m-3\\\\ \\vdots&amp;\\vdots\\\\ (2m-1)^2\\le x&lt;(2m)^2 &amp; 1 \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"134\" />\n</p><p>After the last \\(r=1\\) case, we enter the next interval with remainder\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e17298d708e61f1b3086ef5c8a216a38f96dbff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.\\]\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>That means we arrive exactly at\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a1451414050f15e1ac716938310df85f70bfc7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2m)^2.\\]\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d2821d26bb213174252186b3718ebab5fc58cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\text{the next square after }m^2\\text{ is }(2m)^2.}\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>Moreover, during the process the remainder is always positive, so none of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7fc513cbe9263a26d886e8deba3a7f0a3dff06b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(m+1)^2,(m+2)^2,\\ldots,(2m-1)^2\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>is ever reached.\n</p><p>Hence there are no squares between \\(m^2\\) and \\((2m)^2\\).\n</p><p>This proves the lemma.\n</p><p>Step 3: Apply the lemma repeatedly\n</p><p>We begin with\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d53c2869b259ec933a2e4592eefd1fcce5cd55f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1=1=1^2.\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>By the lemma, the next square is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f578f93eed6f56ecc2c95fe8b882e0d29a684b98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^2.\\]\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Then the next square is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/103b4368395960a4bf75be04ea3c20ab7ad8f0a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2\\cdot2)^2=4^2.\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05a34357f8679b32e973a2e92d94c3632524391e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8^2,\\]\" width=\"20\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d8f3a7becf2a52ab00fa714a6cb987f7c7c54d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16^2,\\]\" width=\"28\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>and so on.\n</p><p>Therefore the square terms are exactly\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b8746c84f7b5bf0c1648a1664c6a761a483f71e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1^2,\\;2^2,\\;4^2,\\;8^2,\\;16^2,\\ldots\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>and hence the corresponding values of \\(m\\) are\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/a/d2ab474211331ffbface63621545c7a90299d835.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{1,2,4,8,16,\\ldots}\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"27\" />\n</p><p>or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/2644198101864ef79ead35694a0c02ef4a478f8c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{m=2^k\\quad\\text{for every integer }k\\ge0}.\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"30\" />\nFinal Answer\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/e/cee181496d6da8569c3447acb71a125f5eeb0347.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\boxed{m=2^k,\\qquad k=0,1,2,\\ldots}}\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO\" title=\"2026 INMO\">2026 INMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indian_National_Mathematical_Olympiad\" title=\"Indian National Mathematical Olympiad\"> All INMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034913\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.630 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 277/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 823/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8626/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   39.828      1 Template:INMO_box\n100.00%   39.828      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36815:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018034913 and revision id 290288. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}